    "result_text": "Done. The test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change belongs in the owner-create pipeline's `assignCustomerCode` step (`src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`), which runs inside the create transaction after `BuildOwner` and before `SaveOwner`. I updated its function class:\n\n**`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`**\n\n- Now injects `OwnerRepository` (matching the pattern of sibling steps `AssignNamesakeCount`, `RejectDuplicateIdentity`, `AssignPossibleDuplicate`).\n- Computes the base `<REGION>-<HASH8>` code via `OwnerCustomerCode.of(...)` as before.\n- Collects the `customerCode`s of all existing owners (skipping the owner being created, which isn't persisted yet).\n- If the base code collides, appends `-<n>` starting at `n = 2` and incrementing until unique (`<base>-2`, then `<base>-3`, \u2026), then sets the de-duplicated code on the owner in place.\n\nThis satisfies the spec: smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique, returning the de-duplicated `customerCode`. It also preserves downstream behaviour \u2014 `OwnerMapper.toLocality` splits on the first `-`, so the REGION segment is unaffected by any appended suffix.\n\nNotes on scope: the suffix only ever appears on a genuine collision (identical region + identical SHA-256 hash of `normalizedTelephone + lastName`), which the acceptance test notes can't be forced black-box since telephone uniqueness feeds the hash. The test therefore asserts the rule's guarantee \u2014 distinct owners get distinct codes \u2014 which passes. The PUT (update) pipeline intentionally does not recompute `customerCode`, so it's unaffected.",
